                "parent_sha256": "79c7e6ed263c4c4b3614880fc69d9c320ff017fcdf08d37be21a3040d8310287",
                "plan": "Output shape equals input shape; contiguous strides all 1. Flat offset = linear index. For n=4099, BLOCK=256 gives 16 programs; last block handles 4096-4098 (3 valid). Mask offsets >= n on load and store. Load as native dtype, cast to fp32, add, cast back to output dtype. Allocate fresh contiguous output via torch.empty_like. No reduction; elementwise. Use BLOCK=256 when n<=8192 else 1024.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, output_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask).to(tl.float32)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask).to(tl.float32)\n    out = (x + y).to(output_ptr.dtype.element_ty)\n    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n_elements = x.numel()\n    if n_elements <= 8192:\n        BLOCK_SIZE = 256\n    else:\n        BLOCK_SIZE = 1024\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n_elements, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    add_kernel[grid](x, y, output, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return output\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: the 4099-element shape is slow because a single 1024-wide block leaves only 4 programs, underutilizing SMs. Observed contradiction: candidate 1.18us vs compiled 0.895us (ratio 0.76) on [4099], while large shapes win. Fix: use a smaller block (256) for small n to increase parallelism; keep 1024 for large n. Coordinate check: flat offset = i; x[i]+y[i] -> out[i]. Edge i=4098: offset 4098, mask true; i=4099 masked out.\",\"plan\":\"Output shape equals input shape; contiguous strides all 1. Flat offset = linear index. For n=4099, BLOCK=256 gives 16 programs; last block handles 4096-4098 (3 valid). Mask offsets >= n on load and store. Load as native dtype, cast to fp32, add, cast back to output dtype. Allocate fresh contiguous output via torch.empty_like. No reduction; elementwise. Use BLOCK=256 when n<=8192 else 1024.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, output_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\",\"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\",\"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = offsets < n_elements\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask).to(tl.float32)\",\"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask).to(tl.float32)\",\"    out = (x + y).to(output_ptr.dtype.element_ty)\",\"    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.shape == y.shape\",\"    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\",\"    output = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    n_elements = x.numel()\",\"    if n_elements <= 8192:\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE = 256\",\"    else:\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE = 1024\",\"    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n_elements, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\",\"    add_kernel[grid](x, y, output, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    return output\"]}",
                "request_id": "baseline-counterexample-r1",
                "source_sha256": "c6228cd7f0eca12d0ac233eba78a363f8e98abf1e6451632c52706186f65e4d8"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, output_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask).to(tl.float32)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask).to(tl.float32)\n    out = (x + y).to(output_ptr.dtype.element_ty)\n    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n_elements = x.numel()\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 1024\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n_elements, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    add_kernel[grid](x, y, output, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return output\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: small shapes are launch-bound; torch.compile wins on 4099. Contradiction: candidate 0.892 vs compiled 0.891 us. Fix: use larger BLOCK_SIZE (1024) to reduce grid/launch overhead for small n. Coordinate check: flat offset i maps to x[i],y[i],out[i]; edge i=4098 valid, i=4099 masked.",
