                "parent_sha256": null,
                "plan": "Padded neutral: mask offsets < n; other=0 for loads. Actual width = n. Mask bounds on load/store. Load as input dtype, cast to fp32, add, cast to input dtype. Allocate torch.empty_like(x). Pass tensors as pointers. Grid = cdiv(n, BLOCK). BLOCK=1024. Return output.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    x_f32 = x.to(tl.float32)\n    y_f32 = y.to(tl.float32)\n    s = x_f32 + y_f32\n    out = s.to(x_ptr.dtype.element_ty)\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\n    assert x.dtype == y.dtype\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 1024\n    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, BLOCK_SIZE),)\n    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Output shape equals x.shape; contiguous strides are 1. Flat offset i maps to x[i], y[i], out[i]. For shape (3,5), coord (2,4) -> flat 14; x[14]+y[14]->out[14]. Edge (0,0)->0. Odd total 15 handled by mask. Inputs immutable; allocate fresh contiguous output.\",\"plan\":\"Padded neutral: mask offsets < n; other=0 for loads. Actual width = n. Mask bounds on load/store. Load as input dtype, cast to fp32, add, cast to input dtype. Allocate torch.empty_like(x). Pass tensors as pointers. Grid = cdiv(n, BLOCK). BLOCK=1024. Return output.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\",\"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\",\"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = offsets < n_elements\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\",\"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\",\"    x_f32 = x.to(tl.float32)\",\"    y_f32 = y.to(tl.float32)\",\"    s = x_f32 + y_f32\",\"    out = s.to(x_ptr.dtype.element_ty)\",\"    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.shape == y.shape\",\"    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\",\"    assert x.dtype == y.dtype\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    n = x.numel()\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = 1024\",\"    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, BLOCK_SIZE),)\",\"    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "initial-contract",
                "source_sha256": "2e0c7803eccdc17226762b12f5edd6c2600d7d3043c3bd5b3632cafd2a064fe2"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    s = x.to(tl.float32) + y.to(tl.float32)\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, s.to(x_ptr.dtype.element_ty), mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\n    assert x.dtype == y.dtype\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 256 if n <= 8192 else 1024\n    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, BLOCK_SIZE),)\n    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return out\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: small-shape launch overhead (4099 bf16: 1.15us vs 0.89us) is the only failing point; large shapes already beat torch.compile. Coordinate check: flat offset = i; for shape (3,5) i=14 -> (2,4) offset 14 in both inputs and output. Fix: reduce per-block work for small n to cut launch/occupancy overhead while keeping FP32 add then cast.",
                "evaluation": {
