                "parent_sha256": "2e0c7803eccdc17226762b12f5edd6c2600d7d3043c3bd5b3632cafd2a064fe2",
                "plan": "Padded neutral: masked loads use other=0.0; masked stores skip padding. Actual width = n; mask = offsets < n. Cast order: load bf16/f32 -> to(f32) -> add -> to(input dtype). Output: torch.empty_like(x) fresh contiguous, same shape/dtype. Grid = cdiv(n, BLOCK). For n<=8192 use BLOCK=256 to reduce per-program overhead; else 1024.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    s = x.to(tl.float32) + y.to(tl.float32)\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, s.to(x_ptr.dtype.element_ty), mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\n    assert x.dtype == y.dtype\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 256 if n <= 8192 else 1024\n    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, BLOCK_SIZE),)\n    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: small-shape launch overhead (4099 bf16: 1.15us vs 0.89us) is the only failing point; large shapes already beat torch.compile. Coordinate check: flat offset = i; for shape (3,5) i=14 -> (2,4) offset 14 in both inputs and output. Fix: reduce per-block work for small n to cut launch/occupancy overhead while keeping FP32 add then cast.\",\"plan\":\"Padded neutral: masked loads use other=0.0; masked stores skip padding. Actual width = n; mask = offsets < n. Cast order: load bf16/f32 -> to(f32) -> add -> to(input dtype). Output: torch.empty_like(x) fresh contiguous, same shape/dtype. Grid = cdiv(n, BLOCK). For n<=8192 use BLOCK=256 to reduce per-program overhead; else 1024.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\",\"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\",\"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = offsets < n_elements\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\",\"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\",\"    s = x.to(tl.float32) + y.to(tl.float32)\",\"    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, s.to(x_ptr.dtype.element_ty), mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.shape == y.shape\",\"    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\",\"    assert x.dtype == y.dtype\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    n = x.numel()\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = 256 if n <= 8192 else 1024\",\"    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, BLOCK_SIZE),)\",\"    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "contract-counterexample-r1",
                "source_sha256": "eeb9ad74eef7dea44a57652ee448358e3959558b9e870fcd5edada940c7ca649"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    s = x.to(tl.float32) + y.to(tl.float32)\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, s.to(x_ptr.dtype.element_ty), mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\n    assert x.dtype == y.dtype\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 512 if n <= 16384 else 1024\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return out\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: small-shape launch overhead and suboptimal block size hurt the 4099-element case (candidate 0.897us vs compiled 0.892us). Contradiction: geometric mean 1.05x requires winning small shapes. Fix: use 512-block for n<=16384 to reduce grid overhead, and use a lambda grid to let Triton specialize BLOCK_SIZE at compile time, avoiding host-side branching cost.",
