                "plan": "Output shape equals input shape; contiguous so flat offset = linear index. For shape [3,5], coord (2,4) maps to offset 14 in both inputs and output. Mask: offsets < n_elements guards odd sizes. Padded lanes load 0.0, add in FP32, cast to element dtype. BLOCK_SIZE=512 for n<=16384, 1024 otherwise. Lambda grid for compile-time specialization.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    s = x.to(tl.float32) + y.to(tl.float32)\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, s.to(x_ptr.dtype.element_ty), mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\n    assert x.dtype == y.dtype\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 512 if n <= 16384 else 1024\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: small-shape launch overhead and suboptimal block size hurt the 4099-element case (candidate 0.897us vs compiled 0.892us). Contradiction: geometric mean 1.05x requires winning small shapes. Fix: use 512-block for n<=16384 to reduce grid overhead, and use a lambda grid to let Triton specialize BLOCK_SIZE at compile time, avoiding host-side branching cost.\",\"plan\":\"Output shape equals input shape; contiguous so flat offset = linear index. For shape [3,5], coord (2,4) maps to offset 14 in both inputs and output. Mask: offsets < n_elements guards odd sizes. Padded lanes load 0.0, add in FP32, cast to element dtype. BLOCK_SIZE=512 for n<=16384, 1024 otherwise. Lambda grid for compile-time specialization.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\",\"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\",\"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = offsets < n_elements\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\",\"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0)\",\"    s = x.to(tl.float32) + y.to(tl.float32)\",\"    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, s.to(x_ptr.dtype.element_ty), mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.shape == y.shape\",\"    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\",\"    assert x.dtype == y.dtype\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    n = x.numel()\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = 512 if n <= 16384 else 1024\",\"    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\",\"    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "contract-counterexample-r2",
