                "plan": "1) Single-pass kernel: accumulate sum and sum-of-squares in one loop. 2) Compute mean and rstd from accumulators. 3) Second loop: normalize, apply weight/bias, store. 4) Host: allocate output, launch with grid=(rows,).",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _layer_norm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    B,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    EVEN: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n    \n    # Single pass: accumulate sum and sum of squares\n    _sum = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    _sum_sq = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        if EVEN:\n            a = tl.load(X + cols).to(tl.float32)\n        else:\n            mask = cols < N\n            a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        _sum += a\n        _sum_sq += a * a\n    sum_val = tl.sum(_sum, axis=0)\n    sum_sq_val = tl.sum(_sum_sq, axis=0)\n    mean = sum_val / N\n    var = sum_sq_val / N - mean * mean\n    rstd = 1 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\n    \n    # Normalize and apply linear transformation\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        if EVEN:\n            w = tl.load(W + cols).to(tl.float32)\n            b = tl.load(B + cols).to(tl.float32)\n            x = tl.load(X + cols).to(tl.float32)\n            x_hat = (x - mean) * rstd\n            y = x_hat * w + b\n            tl.store(Y + cols, y)\n        else:\n            mask = cols < N\n            w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n            b = tl.load(B + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n            x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n            x_hat = (x - mean) * rstd\n            y = x_hat * w + b\n            tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n    \n\ndef run(x, weight, bias):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    EVEN = (width == BLOCK_SIZE)\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _layer_norm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        output,\n        weight,\n        bias,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-5,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n        EVEN=EVEN,\n    )\n    return output\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Fuse mean/var into one pass using Welford-style accumulation to cut memory traffic. Use a single BLOCK_SIZE for all widths; for small widths, one block suffices. Keep FP32 arithmetic, single final cast.\",\"plan\":\"1) Single-pass kernel: accumulate sum and sum-of-squares in one loop. 2) Compute mean and rstd from accumulators. 3) Second loop: normalize, apply weight/bias, store. 4) Host: allocate output, launch with grid=(rows,).\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _layer_norm_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    Y,\",\"    W,\",\"    B,\",\"    stride,\",\"    N,\",\"    eps,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"    EVEN: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\",\"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    X += row * stride\",\"    Y += row * stride\",\"    \",\"    # Single pass: accumulate sum and sum of squares\",\"    _sum = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\",\"    _sum_sq = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        if EVEN:\",\"            a = tl.load(X + cols).to(tl.float32)\",\"        else:\",\"            mask = cols < N\",\"            a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        _sum += a\",\"        _sum_sq += a * a\",\"    sum_val = tl.sum(_sum, axis=0)\",\"    sum_sq_val = tl.sum(_sum_sq, axis=0)\",\"    mean = sum_val / N\",\"    var = sum_sq_val / N - mean * mean\",\"    rstd = 1 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\",\"    \",\"    # Normalize and apply linear transformation\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        if EVEN:\",\"            w = tl.load(W + cols).to(tl.float32)\",\"            b = tl.load(B + cols).to(tl.float32)\",\"            x = tl.load(X + cols).to(tl.float32)\",\"            x_hat = (x - mean) * rstd\",\"            y = x_hat * w + b\",\"            tl.store(Y + cols, y)\",\"        else:\",\"            mask = cols < N\",\"            w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"            b = tl.load(B + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"            x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"            x_hat = (x - mean) * rstd\",\"            y = x_hat * w + b\",\"            tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\",\"    \",\"\",\"def run(x, weight, bias):\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    output = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\",\"    EVEN = (width == BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _layer_norm_kernel[grid](\",\"        x,\",\"        output,\",\"        weight,\",\"        bias,\",\"        width,\",\"        width,\",\"        1e-5,\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\",\"        EVEN=EVEN,\",\"    )\",\"    return output\"]}",
                "request_id": "baseline-baseline-r1",
                "source_sha256": "08b5a80252feaaf4e87b7844b8ea2c48fea680f7f2a19c2ac08b932d3547dad5"
