                "plan": "1. Allocate output tensor. 2. Launch kernel with grid (rows,). 3. Kernel: load row, compute mean/var, normalize, apply weight/bias, store. 4. Use tl.constexpr for BLOCK_SIZE. 5. Mask all loads/stores for odd widths. 6. Return output.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _layer_norm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    B,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n    \n    # Compute mean\n    _mean = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        _mean += a\n    mean = tl.sum(_mean, axis=0) / N\n    \n    # Compute variance\n    _var = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x = tl.where(mask, x - mean, 0.)\n        _var += x * x\n    var = tl.sum(_var, axis=0) / N\n    rstd = 1 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\n    \n    # Normalize and apply linear transformation\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        b = tl.load(B + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x_hat = (x - mean) * rstd\n        y = x_hat * w + b\n        tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n    \n\ndef run(x, weight, bias):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _layer_norm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        output,\n        weight,\n        bias,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-5,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n    )\n    return output\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Fused LayerNorm kernel. One program per row. Loop over width in BLOCK chunks. Compute mean, variance, rstd in FP32. Apply affine transform. Store output. Handle odd widths with masks. Allocate fresh contiguous output.\",\"plan\":\"1. Allocate output tensor. 2. Launch kernel with grid (rows,). 3. Kernel: load row, compute mean/var, normalize, apply weight/bias, store. 4. Use tl.constexpr for BLOCK_SIZE. 5. Mask all loads/stores for odd widths. 6. Return output.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _layer_norm_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    Y,\",\"    W,\",\"    B,\",\"    stride,\",\"    N,\",\"    eps,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\",\"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    X += row * stride\",\"    Y += row * stride\",\"    \",\"    # Compute mean\",\"    _mean = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        _mean += a\",\"    mean = tl.sum(_mean, axis=0) / N\",\"    \",\"    # Compute variance\",\"    _var = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        x = tl.where(mask, x - mean, 0.)\",\"        _var += x * x\",\"    var = tl.sum(_var, axis=0) / N\",\"    rstd = 1 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\",\"    \",\"    # Normalize and apply linear transformation\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        b = tl.load(B + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        x_hat = (x - mean) * rstd\",\"        y = x_hat * w + b\",\"        tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\",\"    \",\"\",\"def run(x, weight, bias):\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    output = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _layer_norm_kernel[grid](\",\"        x,\",\"        output,\",\"        weight,\",\"        bias,\",\"        width,\",\"        width,\",\"        1e-5,\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\",\"    )\",\"    return output\"]}",
                "request_id": "initial-baseline",
                "source_sha256": "dcb2b81c39cfd7bdef2e673d0ea05665c13a358c06190bd545a2efe634206b07"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _layer_norm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    B,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    OUT_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n    \n    # Single-pass Welford mean/var\n    mean = 0.0\n    m2 = 0.0\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        n = tl.sum(tl.where(mask, 1.0, 0.0), axis=0)\n        delta = a - mean\n        mean += tl.sum(delta, axis=0) / n\n        delta2 = a - mean\n        m2 += tl.sum(delta * delta2, axis=0)\n    var = m2 / N\n    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\n    \n    # Fused normalize + affine + store\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        b = tl.load(B + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        y = (x - mean) * rstd * w + b\n        if OUT_BF16:\n            tl.store(Y + cols, y.to(tl.bfloat16), mask=mask)\n        else:\n            tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x, weight, bias):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    out_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _layer_norm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        output,\n        weight,\n        bias,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-5,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n        OUT_BF16=out_bf16,\n    )\n    return output\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: the slowest shape [7,257] bf16 is 1.556us vs 1.269us compiled (0.815x, below 0.90 gate). Contradiction: 3 sequential passes over 257 cols with BLOCK=512 wastes half the lanes and re-reads X three times. Fix: single-pass Welford mean/var, then one fused normalize/store pass, reducing memory traffic and kernel time.",
