                "parent_sha256": "dcb2b81c39cfd7bdef2e673d0ea05665c13a358c06190bd545a2efe634206b07",
                "plan": "Verify coords: row r, col c -> flat r*257+c; edge r=6,c=256 -> 1598. Padded lanes (257..511) masked with other=0.0 so sums divide by N=257. All math FP32; single cast to x.dtype on store. Output torch.empty_like(x) is fresh contiguous same shape/dtype/device. Inputs untouched.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _layer_norm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    B,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    OUT_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n    \n    # Single-pass Welford mean/var\n    mean = 0.0\n    m2 = 0.0\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        n = tl.sum(tl.where(mask, 1.0, 0.0), axis=0)\n        delta = a - mean\n        mean += tl.sum(delta, axis=0) / n\n        delta2 = a - mean\n        m2 += tl.sum(delta * delta2, axis=0)\n    var = m2 / N\n    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\n    \n    # Fused normalize + affine + store\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        b = tl.load(B + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        y = (x - mean) * rstd * w + b\n        if OUT_BF16:\n            tl.store(Y + cols, y.to(tl.bfloat16), mask=mask)\n        else:\n            tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x, weight, bias):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    out_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _layer_norm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        output,\n        weight,\n        bias,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-5,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n        OUT_BF16=out_bf16,\n    )\n    return output\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: the slowest shape [7,257] bf16 is 1.556us vs 1.269us compiled (0.815x, below 0.90 gate). Contradiction: 3 sequential passes over 257 cols with BLOCK=512 wastes half the lanes and re-reads X three times. Fix: single-pass Welford mean/var, then one fused normalize/store pass, reducing memory traffic and kernel time.\",\"plan\":\"Verify coords: row r, col c -> flat r*257+c; edge r=6,c=256 -> 1598. Padded lanes (257..511) masked with other=0.0 so sums divide by N=257. All math FP32; single cast to x.dtype on store. Output torch.empty_like(x) is fresh contiguous same shape/dtype/device. Inputs untouched.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _layer_norm_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    Y,\",\"    W,\",\"    B,\",\"    stride,\",\"    N,\",\"    eps,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"    OUT_BF16: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\",\"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    X += row * stride\",\"    Y += row * stride\",\"    \",\"    # Single-pass Welford mean/var\",\"    mean = 0.0\",\"    m2 = 0.0\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        n = tl.sum(tl.where(mask, 1.0, 0.0), axis=0)\",\"        delta = a - mean\",\"        mean += tl.sum(delta, axis=0) / n\",\"        delta2 = a - mean\",\"        m2 += tl.sum(delta * delta2, axis=0)\",\"    var = m2 / N\",\"    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\",\"    \",\"    # Fused normalize + affine + store\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        b = tl.load(B + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        y = (x - mean) * rstd * w + b\",\"        if OUT_BF16:\",\"            tl.store(Y + cols, y.to(tl.bfloat16), mask=mask)\",\"        else:\",\"            tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x, weight, bias):\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    output = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\",\"    out_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _layer_norm_kernel[grid](\",\"        x,\",\"        output,\",\"        weight,\",\"        bias,\",\"        width,\",\"        width,\",\"        1e-5,\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\",\"        OUT_BF16=out_bf16,\",\"    )\",\"    return output\"]}",
                "request_id": "baseline-counterexample-r1",
                "source_sha256": "69205bbaf9fc3acdad8da3f0d83d25dbd09f6a6768860a9fe4af002a1461af2f"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _layer_norm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    B,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    OUT_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n    \n    # Compute mean\n    _mean = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        _mean += a\n    mean = tl.sum(_mean, axis=0) / N\n    \n    # Compute variance\n    _var = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x = tl.where(mask, x - mean, 0.)\n        _var += x * x\n    var = tl.sum(_var, axis=0) / N\n    rstd = 1 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\n    \n    # Normalize and apply linear transformation\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        b = tl.load(B + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x_hat = (x - mean) * rstd\n        y = x_hat * w + b\n        if OUT_BF16:\n            tl.store(Y + cols, y.to(tl.bfloat16), mask=mask)\n        else:\n            tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n    \n\ndef run(x, weight, bias):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    out_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _layer_norm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        output,\n        weight,\n        bias,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-5,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n        OUT_BF16=out_bf16,\n    )\n    return output\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: the 7x257 bf16 shape is slow because the prior kernel stores FP32 into a bf16 tensor, forcing an implicit per-element cast in the store path. Contradiction: torch.compile fuses the final cast; we must explicitly cast to bf16 before store. Verify: row0 col0 offset 0; row1 col256 offset 257+256=513; mask cols<257 pads 257..255 to 512.",
