                "parent_sha256": "45da787a673b76e5c5448272a6846316dcef67e5c6930a1e52f4bdd688c0d033",
                "plan": "Allocate a fresh contiguous output of shape (rows,) in x.dtype. Launch a single grid over rows. Each program loops over the row in 1024-element chunks, masks the tail, sums in FP32, divides by width, and stores one scalar. No atomics, no extra kernels.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _mean_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    stride_x,\n    width,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    N_CHUNKS: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride_x\n    acc = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for i in tl.static_range(N_CHUNKS):\n        cols = i * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < width\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        acc += x\n    s = tl.sum(acc, axis=0)\n    mean = s / width\n    tl.store(Y + row, mean.to(Y.dtype.element_ty))\n\n\ndef run(x):\n    assert x.is_cuda\n    assert x.dim() == 2\n    assert x.is_contiguous()\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty((rows,), dtype=x.dtype, device=x.device)\n    BLOCK = 1024\n    n_chunks = triton.cdiv(width, BLOCK)\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _mean_kernel[grid](x, out, x.stride(0), width, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK, N_CHUNKS=n_chunks)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Fuse mean into one kernel per row. Use a fixed 1024-wide block and a Python-selected loop count so the compiler specializes per width. Accumulate in FP32, divide by actual width, and store directly in the input dtype. This removes the atomic path and the separate divide/cast kernel.\",\"plan\":\"Allocate a fresh contiguous output of shape (rows,) in x.dtype. Launch a single grid over rows. Each program loops over the row in 1024-element chunks, masks the tail, sums in FP32, divides by width, and stores one scalar. No atomics, no extra kernels.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _mean_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    Y,\",\"    stride_x,\",\"    width,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"    N_CHUNKS: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\", \"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    X += row * stride_x\",\"    acc = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\",\"    for i in tl.static_range(N_CHUNKS):\",\"        cols = i * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < width\",\"        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        acc += x\",\"    s = tl.sum(acc, axis=0)\",\"    mean = s / width\",\"    tl.store(Y + row, mean.to(Y.dtype.element_ty))\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x):\",\"    assert x.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.dim() == 2\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous()\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    out = torch.empty((rows,), dtype=x.dtype, device=x.device)\",\"    BLOCK = 1024\",\"    n_chunks = triton.cdiv(width, BLOCK)\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _mean_kernel[grid](x, out, x.stride(0), width, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK, N_CHUNKS=n_chunks)\",\"    return out\"]}",
