                "parent_sha256": "f019ad1f92200348f2303daaa754727427954627746699543a669d6d7fe50dee",
                "plan": "Check: row r, col c -> offset r*width+c; out[r]=sum_c x[r,c]/width. Edge: r=0,c=0 -> 0; r=0,c=width-1 -> width-1. Padded lanes masked to 0, sum over actual width, divide by width (not block). Cast load to fp32, store to out dtype. Allocate contiguous (rows,) output.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _mean_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    stride_x,\n    width,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride_x\n    Y += row\n    cols = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = cols < width\n    x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n    s = tl.sum(x, axis=0)\n    mean = s / width\n    y = mean.to(Y.dtype.element_ty)\n    tl.store(Y, y)\n\n\ndef run(x):\n    assert x.is_cuda\n    assert x.dim() == 2\n    assert x.is_contiguous()\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty((rows,), dtype=x.dtype, device=x.device)\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _mean_kernel[grid](x, out, x.stride(0), width, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: fixed BLOCK_SIZE=4096 wastes lanes for small widths (e.g. 257), slowing [7,257]. Contradiction: candidate 1.175us > compiled 1.035us. Fix: use next_power_of_2(width) so block matches actual width, reducing wasted threads while preserving masked sum and divide-by-width semantics.\",\"plan\":\"Check: row r, col c -> offset r*width+c; out[r]=sum_c x[r,c]/width. Edge: r=0,c=0 -> 0; r=0,c=width-1 -> width-1. Padded lanes masked to 0, sum over actual width, divide by width (not block). Cast load to fp32, store to out dtype. Allocate contiguous (rows,) output.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _mean_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    Y,\",\"    stride_x,\",\"    width,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\", \"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    X += row * stride_x\",\"    Y += row\",\"    cols = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = cols < width\",\"    x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"    s = tl.sum(x, axis=0)\",\"    mean = s / width\",\"    y = mean.to(Y.dtype.element_ty)\",\"    tl.store(Y, y)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x):\",\"    assert x.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.dim() == 2\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous()\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    out = torch.empty((rows,), dtype=x.dtype, device=x.device)\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _mean_kernel[grid](x, out, x.stride(0), width, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "contract-counterexample-r2",
                "source_sha256": "2a24693b5feb7c24b931b6b79f639365e7df7ae9f3d0f21252c685b6994e33e0"
