                "draft": "Hypothesis: the 7x257 bf16 shape is launch-bound; the grid-stride loop adds overhead. Contradiction: candidate (1.249us) is slower than compiled (1.237us) on the smallest shape. Fix: use one program per row (grid=n_rows) to remove loop overhead, matching the previously validated correct source.",
                "evaluation": {
                  "message": "expected ':' (<unknown>, line 13)",
                  "status": "protocol_error"
                },
                "parent_sha256": "aee5e99ccbaf2c75ad97270fa3d3c44e48617aef1cb466efc14f82597c31f3c7",
                "plan": "Output shape equals input (R,C), contiguous. Offset = r*C+c. Check (0,0)->0 and (0,256)->256 for 7x257. Padded lanes use -inf so exp=0; mask bounds col<C on load/store. FP32 reduction via .to(tl.float32). Cast to bf16 before store. Allocate fresh contiguous output.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _softmax_kernel(\n    input_ptr,\n    output_ptr,\n    n_cols,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n),\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    col_offsets = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = col_offsets < n_cols\n    in_ptrs = input_ptr + row * n_cols + col_offsets\n    row_vals = tl.load(in_ptrs, mask=mask, other=-float('inf'))\n    row_f32 = row_vals.to(tl.float32)\n    row_max = tl.max(row_f32, axis=0)\n    exp_vals = tl.exp(row_f32 - row_max)\n    denom = tl.sum(exp_vals, axis=0)\n    out_vals = exp_vals / denom\n    if IS_BF16:\n        out_vals = out_vals.to(tl.bfloat16)\n    out_ptrs = output_ptr + row * n_cols + col_offsets\n    tl.store(out_ptrs, out_vals, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and x.dim() == 2 and x.is_contiguous()\n    n_rows, n_cols = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(n_cols)\n    grid = (n_rows,)\n    _softmax_kernel[grid](x, out, n_cols, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE, IS_BF16=(x.dtype == torch.bfloat16))\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: the 7x257 bf16 shape is launch-bound; the grid-stride loop adds overhead. Contradiction: candidate (1.249us) is slower than compiled (1.237us) on the smallest shape. Fix: use one program per row (grid=n_rows) to remove loop overhead, matching the previously validated correct source.\",\"plan\":\"Output shape equals input (R,C), contiguous. Offset = r*C+c. Check (0,0)->0 and (0,256)->256 for 7x257. Padded lanes use -inf so exp=0; mask bounds col<C on load/store. FP32 reduction via .to(tl.float32). Cast to bf16 before store. Allocate fresh contiguous output.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _softmax_kernel(\",\"    input_ptr,\",\"    output_ptr,\",\"    n_cols,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\",\"),\",\"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    col_offsets = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = col_offsets < n_cols\",\"    in_ptrs = input_ptr + row * n_cols + col_offsets\",\"    row_vals = tl.load(in_ptrs, mask=mask, other=-float('inf'))\",\"    row_f32 = row_vals.to(tl.float32)\",\"    row_max = tl.max(row_f32, axis=0)\",\"    exp_vals = tl.exp(row_f32 - row_max)\",\"    denom = tl.sum(exp_vals, axis=0)\",\"    out_vals = exp_vals / denom\",\"    if IS_BF16:\",\"        out_vals = out_vals.to(tl.bfloat16)\",\"    out_ptrs = output_ptr + row * n_cols + col_offsets\",\"    tl.store(out_ptrs, out_vals, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and x.dim() == 2 and x.is_contiguous()\",\"    n_rows, n_cols = x.shape\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(n_cols)\",\"    grid = (n_rows,)\",\"    _softmax_kernel[grid](x, out, n_cols, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE, IS_BF16=(x.dtype == torch.bfloat16))\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "baseline-counterexample-r2"
              }
