                "parent_sha256": "e90162c7538953580398399fa813a2ca17f10b17d2d9d0cab6c7527d104207d0",
                "plan": "Output (rows,) contiguous, stride 1. Load X row via row*width, mask cols<width, sum in FP32, divide by actual width, store scalar to Y+row. Allocate fresh contiguous out, cast to x.dtype.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _row_mean_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row\n    acc = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        acc += a\n    total = tl.sum(acc, axis=0)\n    mean = total / N\n    tl.store(Y, mean)\n\n\ndef run(x):\n    assert x.is_cuda\n    assert x.dim() == 2\n    assert x.is_contiguous()\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty((rows,), dtype=x.dtype, device=x.device)\n    if rows == 0 or width == 0:\n        return out\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 1024\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _row_mean_kernel[grid](x, out, width, width, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: the prior kernel passed the row stride (width) as the Y stride, so Y += row*width misaligned output rows. Fix: Y is contiguous (rows,), so Y += row. Verify: row1 col2 offset 5 -> Y offset 1; row0 col0 -> Y offset 0.\",\"plan\":\"Output (rows,) contiguous, stride 1. Load X row via row*width, mask cols<width, sum in FP32, divide by actual width, store scalar to Y+row. Allocate fresh contiguous out, cast to x.dtype.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _row_mean_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    Y,\",\"    stride,\",\"    N,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\",\"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    X += row * stride\",\"    Y += row\",\"    acc = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        acc += a\",\"    total = tl.sum(acc, axis=0)\",\"    mean = total / N\",\"    tl.store(Y, mean)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x):\",\"    assert x.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.dim() == 2\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous()\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    out = torch.empty((rows,), dtype=x.dtype, device=x.device)\",\"    if rows == 0 or width == 0:\",\"        return out\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = 1024\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _row_mean_kernel[grid](x, out, width, width, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "baseline-counterexample-r1",
                "source_sha256": "b7a2b2a69b0fa0e1d0775b47b20bdc3e9c9cc6962ce67a565742b42845e197d9"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _partial_sum_kernel(\n    X,\n    S,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    CHUNK: tl.constexpr,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    chunk = tl.program_id(1)\n    X += row * stride\n    S += row\n    base = chunk * CHUNK\n    acc = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, CHUNK, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = base + off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        acc += a\n    total = tl.sum(acc, axis=0)\n    tl.atomic_add(S, total)\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _finalize_kernel(\n    S,\n    Y,\n    N,\n    OUT_DTYPE: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    s = tl.load(S + row)\n    mean = s / N\n    tl.store(Y + row, mean.to(OUT_DTYPE))\n\n\ndef run(x):\n    assert x.is_cuda\n    assert x.dim() == 2\n    assert x.is_contiguous()\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty((rows,), dtype=x.dtype, device=x.device)\n    if rows == 0 or width == 0:\n        return out\n    s_buf = torch.zeros((rows,), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 1024\n    # Choose chunk size to get reasonable parallelism\n    # For small rows, split width into multiple chunks\n    num_chunks = max(1, min(8, triton.cdiv(width, BLOCK_SIZE)))\n    chunk_size = triton.cdiv(width, num_chunks)\n    # Round chunk_size up to multiple of BLOCK_SIZE for clean loop\n    chunk_size = triton.cdiv(chunk_size, BLOCK_SIZE) * BLOCK_SIZE\n    # Recompute num_chunks based on actual chunk_size\n    num_chunks = triton.cdiv(width, chunk_size)\n    grid1 = (rows, num_chunks)\n    _partial_sum_kernel[grid1](x, s_buf, width, width, chunk_size, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE)\n    grid2 = (rows,)\n    if x.dtype == torch.bfloat16:\n        out_dtype = tl.bfloat16\n    else:\n        out_dtype = tl.float32\n    _finalize_kernel[grid2](s_buf, out, width, OUT_DTYPE=out_dtype)\n    return out\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: single-row grid underutilizes SMs for small rows (e.g., [7,257] slower than compiled). Contradiction: candidate 1.066us vs compiled 1.036us. Fix: split rows into multiple programs along width, use atomic_add for partial sums, then a second kernel to divide by actual width. Coordinate check: row r, col c -> offset r*width+c; output r -> offset r.",
