                "plan": "Output is contiguous same-shape; flat offset i maps to x[i], y[i], out[i]. For n=4099, block 512 gives 8 blocks (last covers 4096..4099, mask handles 3 valid). Use BLOCK_SIZE=512 when n<=8192 else 1024. Load masked, compute in FP32, store once. Allocate fresh contiguous out.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef silu_mul_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    sigmoid_x = 1.0 / (1.0 + tl.exp(-x))\n    result = sigmoid_x * x * y\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, result, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    block = 512 if n <= 8192 else 1024\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    silu_mul_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=block)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: the 4099-element BF16 case is launch-bound; a fixed 1024-wide block wastes a partial block and adds overhead. Observed contradiction: candidate (1.207us) is slower than torch.compile (0.930us) on the smallest shape, while it wins on 65537 and 1048576. Fix: pick a smaller block for tiny n to reduce per-block overhead and tail waste.\",\"plan\":\"Output is contiguous same-shape; flat offset i maps to x[i], y[i], out[i]. For n=4099, block 512 gives 8 blocks (last covers 4096..4099, mask handles 3 valid). Use BLOCK_SIZE=512 when n<=8192 else 1024. Load masked, compute in FP32, store once. Allocate fresh contiguous out.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def silu_mul_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\",\"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\",\"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = offsets < n_elements\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    sigmoid_x = 1.0 / (1.0 + tl.exp(-x))\",\"    result = sigmoid_x * x * y\",\"    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, result, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.shape == y.shape\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    n = x.numel()\",\"    if n == 0:\",\"        return out\",\"    block = 512 if n <= 8192 else 1024\",\"    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\",\"    silu_mul_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=block)\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "baseline-counterexample-r1",
                "source_sha256": "d3af59fe8a083633d3baf8966a005c7d87cbaa672db6a0d7a88d8129d6375830"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef silu_mul_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    sigmoid_x = 1.0 / (1.0 + tl.exp(-x))\n    result = sigmoid_x * x * y\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, result, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    if n <= 8192:\n        block = 256\n    elif n <= 65536:\n        block = 512\n    else:\n        block = 1024\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    silu_mul_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=block)\n    return out\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: small-shape launch overhead and suboptimal block size hurt the 4099-element case (candidate 0.96us vs compiled 0.93us). The 1M case is already 3x faster. For odd sizes like 4099, mask correctly handles the tail. Coordinate check: flat offset i maps to x[i], y[i], out[i] for contiguous tensors; edge i=4098 loads valid, i=4099 masked out.",
                "evaluation": {
                  "checks_passed": 28,
