                "plan": "Keep single-pass masked kernel. Use smaller blocks (128/256) for small n, 1024 for mid, 2048 for large. Set num_warps=4 for small, 8 for large. No dtype args; cast in-kernel to fp32, store once.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef silu_mul_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    sig = tl.sigmoid(x)\n    out = x * sig * y\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = out.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    if n <= 4096:\n        block = 128\n        nw = 4\n    elif n <= 32768:\n        block = 256\n        nw = 4\n    elif n <= 262144:\n        block = 1024\n        nw = 8\n    else:\n        block = 2048\n        nw = 8\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    silu_mul_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=block, num_warps=nw)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Current kernel is correct but small-shape latency is near torch.compile. Tune block sizes and add num_warps to reduce launch/occupancy overhead for small n while keeping large-n throughput.\",\"plan\":\"Keep single-pass masked kernel. Use smaller blocks (128/256) for small n, 1024 for mid, 2048 for large. Set num_warps=4 for small, 8 for large. No dtype args; cast in-kernel to fp32, store once.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def silu_mul_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\",\"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\",\"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = offsets < n_elements\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    sig = tl.sigmoid(x)\",\"    out = x * sig * y\",\"    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.shape == y.shape\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    n = out.numel()\",\"    if n == 0:\",\"        return out\",\"    if n <= 4096:\",\"        block = 128\",\"        nw = 4\",\"    elif n <= 32768:\",\"        block = 256\",\"        nw = 4\",\"    elif n <= 262144:\",\"        block = 1024\",\"        nw = 8\",\"    else:\",\"        block = 2048\",\"        nw = 8\",\"    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\",\"    silu_mul_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=block, num_warps=nw)\",\"    return out\"]}",
