                "plan": "Adapt BLOCK_SIZE to n: small n uses 256 (more blocks, lower latency), large uses 1024. Mask offsets>=n on load/store with other=0.0. Cast x,y to fp32, compute x*sigmoid(x)*y in fp32, store casts to out dtype. Allocate fresh contiguous out via empty_like. Inputs untouched.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef silu_mul_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    sig = tl.sigmoid(x)\n    out = x * sig * y\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = out.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    if n <= 8192:\n        block = 256\n    else:\n        block = 1024\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    silu_mul_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=block)\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: fixed BLOCK_SIZE=1024 underutilizes small shapes (4099 elems -> 4 blocks), adding launch/tail overhead vs torch.compile. Contradiction: 4099 bf16 candidate 1.20us > compiled 0.92us. Coordinate check: flat offset i maps to x[i],y[i],out[i]; edge i=4098 loads x[4098],y[4098], stores out[4098].\",\"plan\":\"Adapt BLOCK_SIZE to n: small n uses 256 (more blocks, lower latency), large uses 1024. Mask offsets>=n on load/store with other=0.0. Cast x,y to fp32, compute x*sigmoid(x)*y in fp32, store casts to out dtype. Allocate fresh contiguous out via empty_like. Inputs untouched.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def silu_mul_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\",\"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\",\"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = offsets < n_elements\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    sig = tl.sigmoid(x)\",\"    out = x * sig * y\",\"    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.shape == y.shape\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    n = out.numel()\",\"    if n == 0:\",\"        return out\",\"    if n <= 8192:\",\"        block = 256\",\"    else:\",\"        block = 1024\",\"    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\",\"    silu_mul_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=block)\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "baseline-counterexample-r1",
                "source_sha256": "9f6cf24ba4eda5fe6fda40afbf04cdb77668da020d4aa9171a1f1d339ae1fc46"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef silu_mul_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    sig = tl.sigmoid(x)\n    out = x * sig * y\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, out, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = out.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    if n <= 4096:\n        block = 256\n    elif n <= 65536:\n        block = 1024\n    else:\n        block = 2048\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']),)\n    silu_mul_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=block)\n    return out\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: the 1M-element shape is DRAM-bound; the prior 1024-wide block underutilizes L2/occupancy. Observed contradiction: candidate already beats torch.compile 3x there, so only a larger, fully-masked vector width can widen the geometric mean. Coordinate check: flat offset i maps to x[i],y[i],out[i]; edge i=n-1 masked when n%BLOCK!=0.",
