                "plan": "Grid=(rows,). Kernel loops over width in BLOCK_SIZE chunks. Accumulate sum of squares in FP32. Compute rstd. Second loop: load x, normalize, cast to dtype, multiply weight, store. Host allocates output, launches kernel.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _rmsnorm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    DTYPE: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n\n    # Compute sum of squares in FP32\n    _sum_sq = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        _sum_sq += a * a\n    sum_sq = tl.sum(_sum_sq, axis=0)\n    mean_sq = sum_sq / N\n    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(mean_sq + eps)\n\n    # Normalize, cast to input dtype, multiply by weight, store\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x_hat = x * rstd\n        x_hat = x_hat.to(DTYPE)\n        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask)\n        y = w * x_hat\n        tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x, weight):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    if BLOCK_SIZE > 4096:\n        BLOCK_SIZE = 4096\n\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        out,\n        weight,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-6,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n        DTYPE=x.dtype,\n    )\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"RMSNorm kernel: one program per row. Load x in FP32, compute mean of squares over width (masked), rstd=rsqrt(mean+eps). Normalize, cast to input dtype, multiply by weight, store. Handle odd widths via masking.\",\"plan\":\"Grid=(rows,). Kernel loops over width in BLOCK_SIZE chunks. Accumulate sum of squares in FP32. Compute rstd. Second loop: load x, normalize, cast to dtype, multiply weight, store. Host allocates output, launches kernel.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _rmsnorm_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    Y,\",\"    W,\",\"    stride,\",\"    N,\",\"    eps,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"    DTYPE: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\",\"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    X += row * stride\",\"    Y += row * stride\",\"\",\"    # Compute sum of squares in FP32\",\"    _sum_sq = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        _sum_sq += a * a\",\"    sum_sq = tl.sum(_sum_sq, axis=0)\",\"    mean_sq = sum_sq / N\",\"    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(mean_sq + eps)\",\"\",\"    # Normalize, cast to input dtype, multiply by weight, store\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        x_hat = x * rstd\",\"        x_hat = x_hat.to(DTYPE)\",\"        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask)\",\"        y = w * x_hat\",\"        tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x, weight):\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\",\"    if BLOCK_SIZE > 4096:\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE = 4096\",\"\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\",\"        x,\",\"        out,\",\"        weight,\",\"        width,\",\"        width,\",\"        1e-6,\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\",\"        DTYPE=x.dtype,\",\"    )\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "initial-baseline",
                "source_sha256": "911c39ebea1e77536d8b7005af79793844af5c5d3af5e0bee7b53afcfdcc1558"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _rmsnorm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n\n    # Pass 1: sum of squares in FP32\n    _sum_sq = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        _sum_sq += a * a\n    sum_sq = tl.sum(_sum_sq, axis=0)\n    mean_sq = sum_sq / N\n    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(mean_sq + eps)\n\n    # Pass 2: normalize, cast to input dtype, multiply by weight, store\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x_hat = x * rstd\n        if IS_BF16:\n            x_hat = x_hat.to(tl.bfloat16)\n        else:\n            x_hat = x_hat.to(tl.float32)\n        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask)\n        y = w * x_hat\n        tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x, weight):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    if BLOCK_SIZE > 4096:\n        BLOCK_SIZE = 4096\n\n    is_bf16 = 1 if x.dtype == torch.bfloat16 else 0\n\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        out,\n        weight,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-6,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n        IS_BF16=is_bf16,\n    )\n    return out\n",
                "draft": "RMSNorm kernel: compute sum-of-squares in FP32, rstd, normalize, cast to input dtype, multiply by weight. Two-pass over row with masking for odd widths.",
