                "plan": "Allocate contiguous out. Use next_power_of_2 for BLOCK. Mask loads/stores for odd N. Sum squares in FP32, divide by actual N. Cast normalized to input dtype via store. Multiply by weight. Grid rows.",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _rmsnorm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n),\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n\n    _sum_sq = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        _sum_sq += a * a\n    sum_sq = tl.sum(_sum_sq, axis=0)\n    mean_sq = sum_sq / N\n    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(mean_sq + eps)\n\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x_hat = x * rstd\n        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask)\n        y = w * x_hat\n        tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x, weight):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    if BLOCK_SIZE > 4096:\n        BLOCK_SIZE = 4096\n\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        out,\n        weight,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-6,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n    )\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Hypothesis: passing DTYPE as a runtime arg fails; pointer encodes dtype. Contradiction: compile error at .to(DTYPE). Fix: remove DTYPE param; let tl.store cast. Verify: row0 col0 offset 0; row1 col0 offset width. Padded cols masked to 0.\",\"plan\":\"Allocate contiguous out. Use next_power_of_2 for BLOCK. Mask loads/stores for odd N. Sum squares in FP32, divide by actual N. Cast normalized to input dtype via store. Multiply by weight. Grid rows.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _rmsnorm_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    Y,\",\"    W,\",\"    stride,\",\"    N,\",\"    eps,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"),\",\"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    X += row * stride\",\"    Y += row * stride\",\"\",\"    _sum_sq = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        _sum_sq += a * a\",\"    sum_sq = tl.sum(_sum_sq, axis=0)\",\"    mean_sq = sum_sq / N\",\"    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(mean_sq + eps)\",\"\",\"    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\",\"        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"        mask = cols < N\",\"        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\",\"        x_hat = x * rstd\",\"        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask)\",\"        y = w * x_hat\",\"        tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x, weight):\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\",\"    if BLOCK_SIZE > 4096:\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE = 4096\",\"\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\",\"        x,\",\"        out,\",\"        weight,\",\"        width,\",\"        width,\",\"        1e-6,\",\"        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\",\"    )\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "baseline-counterexample-r1"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _rmsnorm_kernel(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    W,\n    stride,\n    N,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    X += row * stride\n    Y += row * stride\n\n    _sum_sq = tl.zeros([BLOCK_SIZE], dtype=tl.float32)\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        a = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        _sum_sq += a * a\n    sum_sq = tl.sum(_sum_sq, axis=0)\n    mean_sq = sum_sq / N\n    rstd = 1.0 / tl.sqrt(mean_sq + eps)\n\n    for off in range(0, N, BLOCK_SIZE):\n        cols = off + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n        mask = cols < N\n        x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=mask, other=0.).to(tl.float32)\n        x_hat = x * rstd\n        if IS_BF16:\n            x_hat = x_hat.to(tl.bfloat16)\n        else:\n            x_hat = x_hat.to(tl.float32)\n        w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask)\n        y = w * x_hat\n        tl.store(Y + cols, y, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x, weight):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n\n    BLOCK_SIZE = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    if BLOCK_SIZE > 4096:\n        BLOCK_SIZE = 4096\n\n    is_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        out,\n        weight,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-6,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n        IS_BF16=is_bf16,\n    )\n    return out\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: the previous source had a syntax error (missing colon after the kernel signature) causing a protocol/compile failure. The observed contradiction is the 'expected :' at line 15. Coordinate check: for x[0,0] offset=0; for x[1,0] offset=width. Output y[r,c] = weight[c] * (x[r,c].float() * rsqrt(mean(x[r,:].float()^2)+eps)).to(dtype).",
