                "parent_sha256": null,
                "plan": "Pad width to power-of-two BLOCK. Mask cols<width on loads/stores. Use other=0.0 for x so masked contribute zero to sum. Divide sum by actual width (not BLOCK). Compute rstd in fp32. Cast normalized to x.dtype before multiplying by weight. Allocate fresh contiguous out via torch.empty_like. Grid=(rows,).",
                "proposed_code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _rmsnorm_kernel(\n    X,\n    W,\n    Y,\n    stride_x,\n    stride_y,\n    width,\n    eps,\n    BLOCK: tl.constexpr,\n    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    x_ptr = X + row * stride_x\n    y_ptr = Y + row * stride_y\n    cols = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    mask = cols < width\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + cols, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    x2 = x * x\n    sum_x2 = tl.sum(x2, axis=0)\n    mean_x2 = sum_x2 / width\n    rstd = tl.rsqrt(mean_x2 + eps)\n    normalized = x * rstd\n    if IS_BF16:\n        normalized = normalized.to(tl.bfloat16)\n    else:\n        normalized = normalized.to(tl.float32)\n    w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    y = w * normalized\n    tl.store(y_ptr + cols, y, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x, weight):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    BLOCK = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    is_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\n    grid = (rows,)\n    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        weight,\n        out,\n        width,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-6,\n        BLOCK=BLOCK,\n        IS_BF16=is_bf16,\n    )\n    return out\n",
                "reply": "{\"draft\":\"Output shape (rows,width), contiguous. Row r, col c: out[r,c]=w[c]*((x[r,c].float()*rsqrt(mean(x[r,:].float()^2)+1e-6)).to(dtype)). Strides: x/out stride=width, w stride=1. Flat offsets: x=r*width+c, w=c, out=r*width+c. Check r=0,c=0 and r=1,c=width-1 for odd width=3: offsets 0,2 and 3,5.\",\"plan\":\"Pad width to power-of-two BLOCK. Mask cols<width on loads/stores. Use other=0.0 for x so masked contribute zero to sum. Divide sum by actual width (not BLOCK). Compute rstd in fp32. Cast normalized to x.dtype before multiplying by weight. Allocate fresh contiguous out via torch.empty_like. Grid=(rows,).\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _rmsnorm_kernel(\",\"    X,\",\"    W,\",\"    Y,\",\"    stride_x,\",\"    stride_y,\",\"    width,\",\"    eps,\",\"    BLOCK: tl.constexpr,\",\"    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\",\"    row = tl.program_id(0)\",\"    x_ptr = X + row * stride_x\",\"    y_ptr = Y + row * stride_y\",\"    cols = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\",\"    mask = cols < width\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + cols, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    x2 = x * x\",\"    sum_x2 = tl.sum(x2, axis=0)\",\"    mean_x2 = sum_x2 / width\",\"    rstd = tl.rsqrt(mean_x2 + eps)\",\"    normalized = x * rstd\",\"    if IS_BF16:\",\"        normalized = normalized.to(tl.bfloat16)\",\"    else:\",\"        normalized = normalized.to(tl.float32)\",\"    w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.0)\",\"    y = w * normalized\",\"    tl.store(y_ptr + cols, y, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x, weight):\",\"    rows, width = x.shape\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    BLOCK = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\",\"    is_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\",\"    grid = (rows,)\",\"    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\",\"        x,\",\"        weight,\",\"        out,\",\"        width,\",\"        width,\",\"        width,\",\"        1e-6,\",\"        BLOCK=BLOCK,\",\"        IS_BF16=is_bf16,\",\"    )\",\"    return out\"]}",
                "request_id": "initial-contract",
                "source_sha256": "0ef65c9dc42f4835d7ffb3537b77b4c2503f58baed5120c1159d54224daa6e74"
              },
              {
                "code": "import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _rmsnorm_kernel(\n    X,\n    W,\n    Y,\n    stride_x,\n    stride_y,\n    width,\n    eps,\n    ROWS_PER_BLOCK: tl.constexpr,\n    BLOCK: tl.constexpr,\n    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    pid = tl.program_id(0)\n    cols = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    mask = cols < width\n    w = tl.load(W + cols, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n    for i in range(ROWS_PER_BLOCK):\n        row = pid * ROWS_PER_BLOCK + i\n        x_ptr = X + row * stride_x\n        y_ptr = Y + row * stride_y\n        x = tl.load(x_ptr + cols, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n        x2 = x * x\n        sum_x2 = tl.sum(x2, axis=0)\n        mean_x2 = sum_x2 / width\n        rstd = tl.rsqrt(mean_x2 + eps)\n        normalized = x * rstd\n        if IS_BF16:\n            normalized = normalized.to(tl.bfloat16)\n        else:\n            normalized = normalized.to(tl.float32)\n        y = w * normalized\n        tl.store(y_ptr + cols, y, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x, weight):\n    rows, width = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    BLOCK = triton.next_power_of_2(width)\n    is_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\n    if rows <= 8:\n        rpb = triton.cdiv(rows, 1)\n        grid = (1,)\n    elif rows <= 32:\n        rpb = 4\n        grid = (triton.cdiv(rows, rpb),)\n    else:\n        rpb = 8\n        grid = (triton.cdiv(rows, rpb),)\n    _rmsnorm_kernel[grid](\n        x,\n        weight,\n        out,\n        width,\n        width,\n        width,\n        1e-6,\n        ROWS_PER_BLOCK=rpb,\n        BLOCK=BLOCK,\n        IS_BF16=is_bf16,\n    )\n    return out\n",
                "draft": "Hypothesis: the slowest shape [7,257] bf16 is launch-bound; the single-row-per-block grid underutilizes the GPU. Contradiction: candidate 1.20us vs compiled 1.13us. Fix: process multiple rows per block to reduce launch overhead for small row counts.",
